# ax web UI — rebuild required after changes

> **ABSOLUTE**: `npm run build` in `crates/ax-web/web-ui/` alone is **not** enough. The UI is embedded into the `ax` binary at compile time (`include_dir!("web-ui/dist")`). Agents must rebuild and reinstall `ax` before telling the user to preview `ax web`.

## When this applies

Any change under `crates/ax-web/web-ui/` (React pages, CSS, components, `dist/` output).

## Required workflow (end of every ax-web UI task)

```text
1. npm run build          # in crates/ax-web/web-ui/ (also runs via ax-web build.rs)
2. .\scripts\release-local.ps1   # or cargo build --release -p ax-cli
3. Reinstall verified: ax --version + (Get-Command ax).Source
4. Restart ax web         # kill old process; ax web --open
5. Tell user: hard refresh browser (Ctrl+Shift+R) if layout still looks stale
```

On macOS/Linux use `bash scripts/reinstall-cli.sh` or `scripts/release-local.ps1` equivalent.

## Forbidden

- Reporting UI work as done after only `npm run build`
- Asking the user to refresh `ax web` without rebuilding the `ax` binary
- Testing UI changes with a stale `ax web` process serving an old embedded bundle

## Verify

- Vite output filenames changed in `web-ui/dist/index.html` (hashed assets)
- `ax-web` crate recompiled in the release build log
- User sees new layout after restart + hard refresh
